    Bug 2037733 - Fix non-threaded subject sorting to group replies with originals. r=BenC


    Bug 2022456 introduced a regression where sorting by Subject in a
    non-threaded view separated original messages from their replies. This
    occurred because `nsMsgDBView::GetCollationKey` began using `FetchSubject()`,
    which explicitly prepends "Re: " to the collation key if the `HasRe` flag
    is set. As a result, all replies were forcibly grouped together under 'R'
    rather than sorting alphabetically alongside their core subjects.

    This patch modifies `GetCollationKey` for `nsMsgViewSortType::bySubject`
    to directly call `GetMime2DecodedSubject()`, bypassing `FetchSubject()`.
    This restores the expected behavior where original messages and their
    "Re:" prefixed replies generate the same base collation key and are
    grouped adjacently in alphabetical sorts.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D299096

diff --git a/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgDBView.cpp b/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgDBView.cpp
index a086b091a36..7a05d43f211 100644
--- a/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgDBView.cpp
+++ b/mailnews/base/src/nsMsgDBView.cpp
@@ -3529,17 +3529,13 @@ nsresult nsMsgDBView::GetCollationKey(nsIMsgDBHdr* msgHdr,
   NS_ENSURE_ARG_POINTER(msgHdr);

   switch (sortType) {
-    case nsMsgViewSortType::bySubject: {
-      uint32_t flags;
-      msgHdr->GetFlags(&flags);
-      rv = FetchSubject(msgHdr, flags, result);
+    case nsMsgViewSortType::bySubject:
+      rv = msgHdr->GetMime2DecodedSubject(result);
       break;
-    }
     case nsMsgViewSortType::byLocation:
       rv = GetLocationCollationKey(msgHdr, result);
       break;
     case nsMsgViewSortType::byRecipient: {
-      nsString recipients;
       rv = FetchRecipients(msgHdr, result);
       break;
     }
